{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R4LXRjv53QDtuRhroQqW3g","type":"tool_result","content":"1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seco\n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1118:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1119:- `talk.game`: its game\n1120:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1121:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1122:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1123:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1124:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1125:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1126:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1127:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1128:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1129:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n1130:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n1131:- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n1132:- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n1133:- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df8c1585-be07-48c4-a448-ca4232e59bdf","uuid":"5c87c597-aa46-4090-b795-eb2c2b4b25be","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:18:17.958Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seco\n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's