{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7cLcNcfavSmZMCTJWz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JckB8weQMY5DwJAnh3qEfs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/x22cc1b-dl/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 833,843p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300; grep -n \"noise2\\|^- \\`E.tones\\|^- \\`E.hash\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-200 | head; grep -n \"^- \\`game.saves\\|^- \\`saves\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-200 | head -20","description":"Check texture helpers, noise, saves APIs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":991,"cache_read_input_tokens":130728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":991,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df8c1585-be07-48c4-a448-ca4232e59bdf","uuid":"f1f69d75-f978-46f3-830e-7f5f22dd2a09","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:20:38.707Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7cLEo4fHRoCaNVJA17","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JckB8weQMY5DwJAnh3qEfs":{"command":"cd /tmp/x22cc1b-dl/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 833,843p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300; grep -n \"noise2\\|^- \\`E.tones\\|^- \\`E.hash\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-200 | head; grep -n \"^- \\`game.saves\\|^- \\`saves\\.\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-200 | head -20","description":"Check texture helpers, noise, saves APIs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JckB8weQMY5DwJAnh3qEfs","type":"tool_result","content":"## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n\n- `E.tex`: floor textures for a TileMap's floorTex(x, y), each giving [r, g, b] at a world point; as materials too: floorMat: 'grass'\n- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n- `E.tex.dirt(x, y, o = {})`: dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light }\n- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n- `E.tex.planks(x, y, o = {})`: wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line }\n- `E.tex.water(x, y, o = {})`: water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light }\n\n162:- `E.hash2(x, y)`: a fixed random number 0..1 for whole-number grid coordinates (texture specks, scatter that never flickers)\n171:- `E.noise2(x, y)`: smooth value noise 0..1 over the plane (one bump per whole unit): blotches, clouds, wobble\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, defa\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, \n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the s\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: bl\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless ga\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df8c1585-be07-48c4-a448-ca4232e59bdf","uuid":"231778cb-e555-438b-a848-13c22cd701a2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:20:38.860Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n\n- `E.tex`: floor textures for a TileMap's floorTex(x, y), each giving [r, g, b] at a world point; as materials too: floorMat: 'grass'\n- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n- `E.tex.dirt(x, y, o = {})`: dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light }\n- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n- `E.tex.planks(x, y, o = {})`: wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line }\n- `E.tex.water(x, y, o = {})`: water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light }\n\n162:- `E.hash2(x, y)`: a fixed random number 0..1 for whole-number grid coordinates (texture specks, scatter that never flickers)\n171:- `E.noise2(x, y)`: smooth value noise 0..1 over the plane (one bump per whole unit): blotches, clouds, wobble\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, defa\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, \n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the s\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: bl\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless ga\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JckB8weQMY5DwJAnh3qEfs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
