 with a state dump beside them: they showed layout, readability and AI state at once.'],\",\"-    ['Least helpful', 'Full-length waits for timed events (the lieutenant\\\\'s pickup) in a real-time browser; reading the state handle was faster.']\",\"+    ['Issues caught', '12: the camera not following during the first briefing, center lines drawn as yellow squares, unreadable heat badges, a missing middle-dot glyph, the case board overflowing a 240-pixel screen, the minimize prompt naming Escape (which pauses), a crash pinning a photo, fiends stuck behind buildings, the player car missing its body at the pier, the heat panel under the touch menu button, the wall clock over the room title, and a syntax error from a bad text edit.'],\",\"+    ['Critical', '3 were game breaking: the crash when pinning a photo (chapter 3 could not be finished), fiends stuck on buildings (the corner could stall), and the syntax error (a blank page).'],\",\"+    ['Most helpful', 'Scripted playthroughs that pressed through dialogs like a player and read the game state after each step: they found the board crash and the stuck fiends.'],\",\"+    ['Least helpful', 'Waiting in real time for timed events in the browser; reading the state handle told me the same thing faster.']\",\"   ] },\",\"   { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK', rows: [\",\"     ['Liked most', 'Sight, suspicion and sight cones (E.sees, E.Suspicion, r.sightCone) work together out of the box, and dialogs with live portraits made the cast feel real for free.'],\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181310__xac1bf5/work/WireMeUp-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181310/game.js\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":1849,\"oldLines\":10,\"newStart\":1849,\"newLines\":10,\"lines\":[\"     ['Usage', 'unknown']\",\"   ] },\",\"   { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', rows: [\",\"-    ['Issues caught', '9 issues caught by testing.'],\",\"-    ['Critical', '3 would have been game breaking: the camera not follow